* Marshall AFD100, Eco preamp, part 1 of 3: V5 and its coupling / volume network. Same circuit as
* preamp.net (see its header), cut where V5's plate drives the volume pot. The next part repeats the
* coupling network, so V6A's grid conduction acts through the real source impedance there; this part
* sees V6A's grid as open (apart from its 150k load in AFD mode).
*
* The rails of the parts that are not here are replaced by equivalent loads from the whole circuit's
* DC solution (tests/data/afd100_preamp_full.net, rail 467.4 V): V8 on HT4, V7 on HT5, V6 on HT6.

.nodes x h4 h5 h6 h7 in g5 p5 k5 c61 v1t v1w n6a

V VRAIL x 100 400
R R61 x h4 10k
C C50 h4 0 47u
R R_V8 h4 0 143.1k
R R60 h4 h5 10k
C C44 h5 0 47u
R R_V7 h5 0 99.8k
R R59 h5 h6 10k
C C47 h6 0 47u
R R_V6 h6 0 523k
R R58 h6 h7 10k
C C42 h7 0 47u

I VIN gin 1
R RSRC gin in 7k
* The guitar behind its source impedance. RSRC is the plain 7k source: the "Off" setting, and what a pedal in front of the amp
* looks like. A pickup replaces it with its own impedance as seen from the open-circuit voltage (the recording): the
* coil (winding resistance RPU + inductance) in parallel with its winding capacitance CPU and an eddy-current loss resistor
* RPL, then the cable capacitance (200 pF per 2 m, switched in steps of 200, 400 and 800 pF). The engine sets the values:
* single coil = coil 1 (2.5 H), humbucker and P-90 = coil 2 (5 H) with their own resistances; open = 1e12.
R RPU1 gin pkb1 1e12
.xfmr LPU1 L=2.5
  W pkb1 in 1 pu
.end
R RPU2 gin pkb2 1e12
.xfmr LPU2 L=5
  W pkb2 in 1 pu
.end
C CPU gin in 110p
R RPL gin in 1e12
R SWK1 in pkk1 1e12
C CCAB1 pkk1 0 200p
R SWK2 in pkk2 1e12
C CCAB2 pkk2 0 400p
R SWK4 in pkk4 1e12
C CCAB4 pkk4 0 800p
R R121 in 0 1M
R R119 in g5 68k
R R88 g5 0 4M7

T V5 g5 p5 k5 12AX7 2
R R72 h7 p5 51k
R R113 k5 0 1.33k
C C74 k5 0 680n
C C75 k5 0 680n
C C46 p5 k5 220p

C C61 p5 c61 22n
R R89 c61 v1t 470k
C C70 c61 v1t 2.2n
R VR1_T v1t v1w 1
R VR1_B v1w 0 1
C C80 v1t v1w 1n

* V6A's grid leak in AFD mode (RL3B closed): the 150k load on the volume wiper.
R R80 v1w n6a 150k
R SW_RL3B n6a 0 1e12
